Every claim here was verified by installing the plugin with the real
codex-cli 0.153.4, in an isolated CODEX_HOME and again in a fresh
CreateOS sandbox (14/14 assertions).

Findings that drove the design:
- Scoped plugin names are refused outright, so the previously documented
  install command could never have worked.
- The hook wire format is identical to Claude Code's, so the previous
  echo-based hook was silently a no-op.
- Symlinking the shared driver and skill installs a plugin with NEITHER:
  the installer copies regular files only, and reports success. Hence
  real copies plus a CI drift check.
- manifest.json declared name createos-sandbox, colliding with the Claude
  Code plugin's id; realigned to createos-sandbox-codex.

Known, not fixed here: both hooks begin 'command -v jq || exit 0', so on a
host without jq they emit zero bytes and the agent never learns the driver
path — the ADR-0001 fail-open, reintroduced by a dependency. Affects the
Claude Code plugin identically.
